ok - objective to audit to worker to plan to worker to completion flows through every phase
ok - the plan consultation explicitly carries objective, context, audit result, and worker findings
ok - a ChatGPT bridge failure exits nonzero, records last_error, keeps the phase, and dispatches nothing
ok - a worker failure returns to dispatch, records last_error, and the stage retries
ok - a failed spawn records last_error, holds the dispatch phase, and the stage retries
ok - dispatch refuses option-leading and batch first args, and hands off with an explicit FM_HOME
ok - wrong-phase calls refuse with no state change
ok - every subcommand validates the task id before building state paths
ok - a trailing valueless option refuses with a usage error instead of hanging
ok - bridge lifecycle stays Firstmate-owned: dispatch refuses a bridge-referencing arg before launch and reports the bridge itself
ok - bridge start and stop verify the recorded pid against the daemon-dir entrypoints before refusing or killing
ok - bridge install and setup verbs and any extra start/stop argument refuse
ok - the audit worker receives the banner-stripped ChatGPT-generated prompt while the objective stays in loop state for the plan packet
ok - the consult receipt strips only a leading Local-tools-unavailable blockquote and preserves every other byte
ok - dispatch carries the selected per-stage effort in the worker argv and keeps low as the audit default
ok - a plan consult citing a usable prior audit records it and skips the redundant audit worker
ok - a task stuck at audit-worker plans directly from cited prior audit evidence
ok - a plan consult without cited prior audit evidence keeps the normal audit-required path
ok - malformed or missing cited evidence is rejected with the phase intact and the stage retryable
ok - a successful audit records non-empty findings while an empty record never completes the worker
ok - the completion path resolves the dispatched worker's report so findings stop staying empty
ok - effort reaches the spawn once, from whichever single source supplied it, and conflicting sources refuse
